# SINO WEALTH USB touchpad keyboard (258a:6a88) — start the per-device scroll
# inverter when the pointer half of it appears.
#
# WHY A UDEV RULE AND NOT A PLAIN ENABLED UNIT: this is a USB keyboard that gets
# plugged and unplugged, and its event node number is whatever the kernel hands
# out that boot. A statically enabled service would have to guess the path at
# boot and would be wrong the first time anything else enumerated ahead of it.
# udev knows the node, so it passes it in as the instance name.
#
# ID_INPUT_MOUSE=="1" IS LOAD-BEARING. This keyboard presents TWO event nodes
# under the same VID/PID:
#
#   event7  ID_INPUT_KEYBOARD=1               the keys
#   event8  ID_INPUT_MOUSE=1, ID_INPUT_KEY=1  the touchpad (plus some keys)
#
# Only the second one has a wheel. Without this match the rule would fire for
# both and the inverter would be handed the keyboard — which it refuses (it
# checks for REL_WHEEL before grabbing anything), but the refusal would be a
# recurring journal error rather than a thing that never happens.
#
# Matched on VID/PID rather than the device name string: the name is a firmware
# field and these no-name pads are re-badged freely, while the ids are what the
# udev database is keyed on anyway.
ACTION=="add", SUBSYSTEM=="input", KERNEL=="event*", \
  ENV{ID_VENDOR_ID}=="258a", ENV{ID_MODEL_ID}=="6a88", ENV{ID_INPUT_MOUSE}=="1", \
  TAG+="systemd", ENV{SYSTEMD_WANTS}+="kb3lyb-natural-scroll@%k.service"
